      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Second inversion",
      "body": "Take E G C and move the E up an octave: G C E. Now the 5th is lowest. That is **second inversion**.\n\n**Why it matters:** Second inversion is the handiest layout for many changes: C in second inversion to F in root position moves only two fingers, by a step each.",
